Decision rule (pre-fixed):
- SC1 SUPPORTED iff (KR quote set Q_KR all found in KR source) — threshold stated for AF data.
- SC2 PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED iff LR quote set found (rates + sigma + AF) — because source rates are o(r^{-1-σ})/o(r^{-2-σ}) (strictly faster than the schema's O(r^{-1})/O(r^{-2})) and derivative counts are not given.
- SC3 NOT_FOUND_IN_CHECKED_SET iff none of the exact normalization patterns occur in any checked source AND at least one checked source uses a *different* weighted-space convention (BI quote found).
- SC4 NOT_FOUND_IN_CHECKED_SET iff the interval pattern is absent.
- overall: PARTIAL (no SC3/SC4 support) → do NOT clear the UNVERIFIED flag.
- The checker FAILS (exit 1) if integrity or required quotes are missing.

